        "title": "Aquaculture - Farmed Seafood Production, Systems, Species, Sustainability",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Aquaculture surpassed wild-catch fishing as the primary source of fish for human consumption around 2014. It now provides ~57% of seafood consumed globally and is the fastest-growing food production sector. But aquaculture systems span an enormous range — from low-intensity oyster beds that actively filter and clean water, to high-density salmon net pens that concentrate waste and require continuous antibiotic management, to recirculating aquaculture systems (RAS) that are essentially liquid factories. Understanding which system produces what, at what cost, is the framework."
